Williams’s qualitative risk rule is: $\text{if every investment succeeds}
\;\Longrightarrow\;
\text{the risk meter may be too low}.$ This is not a probability model. It is a warning that avoiding every loss can also mean avoiding enough uncertainty to create meaningful upside.

