p.src:
The alignment term matters on boards as much as in investments. Williams wants people working toward making the play successful, not merely becoming the brightest light in the room. That adds a practical correction to the book’s risk chapter: risk appetite and character diligence have to be held together. $\text{risk fit}
=
\text{uncertainty accepted}
+
\text{people understood}
+
\text{goals aligned}.$

